# CODEOWNERS

# The lab uses a single-maintainer model (see ADR-0002). The
# required-approving-review count is currently 0; the moment a
# second maintainer is added, this file is the source of truth
# for who must approve a PR. Each line is a path pattern and a
# GitHub user/team handle. The last match wins, so put more
# specific rules after the catch-all.

# Default: the single maintainer owns everything.
* @vonstegen

# Workflow changes require explicit review because they
# control what gets built and which secrets are exposed.
/.github/workflows/ @vonstegen
/.github/dependabot.yml @vonstegen

# Decisions are append-only; require a second pair of eyes
# when a second maintainer joins.
/docs/decisions/ @vonstegen

# baseline/ is a snapshot of upstream; changes there must be
# driven by a documented upstream-sync topic branch (see
# docs/WORKFLOW.md).
/baseline/ @vonstegen
